=== PHASE 3: SEMANTIC BLOCK - how it was built ===
Similarity space: a separate encoder (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) on each of the 50,257 token strings.
Rejected: distilgpt2's own input-embedding matrix. Its nearest tokens to the topic are
" and", " the", ",", " in" (frequency, not meaning).
Rejected: raw MiniLM similarity alone. " and" (0.111) scores above "redients" (0.110), so
no threshold separates topic fragments from function words.
Used: topic SPECIFICITY = sim(cooking) - max sim(7 control topics: politics, sports,
computing, weather, finance, music, travel); block if > 0 and sim > vocab median.
-> 5675 tokens (11.3% of vocab). " the" -0.120, " a" -0.092, " and" -0.080, " council"
-0.344 stay allowed. " nut", "inkle", " olive", " Stew", " Plum", " coconut", " marg"
(borderline +0.001) are blocked. Single subword fragments are still not recognised
("redients" -0.018, " palm", " ground", " Pour"), so the Phase 2 list is added on top:
6319 blocked in total. The init filler " x" (+0.005, noise) is exempt so every run
starts from the same point.

=== PHASE 3 RESULTS ===
SA (band + semantic): the band is reached (0.1722 at step 10, then frozen) but the
   continuation stays fully OFF-TOPIC: MiniLM 0.895, 0 keywords, "The City Council will
   meet on Tuesday, May 6 ...". Measure (1) is satisfied and measure (2) fails completely.
S  (min + semantic): measure (1) falls as far as without any block (0.1205 vs 0.118).
   Measure (2) stays off-topic for the first 25 steps (MiniLM 0.79-0.99) although the
   state is already inside/below the band (0.165 -> 0.141). It turns topical only from
   ~step 100 ("and bake for 2-3 minutes"), ending at MiniLM 0.415 with 1 keyword in 11
   words ("try this recipe:").
   No final suffix token is topic-specific per MiniLM (max spec -0.007). But read by a
   human, the suffix is recipe-INSTRUCTION register: "Heat", "thinly", "mins", "repeat",
   "Spin", "bou", "grueced". These words are not cooking-specific one by one (heat ->
   weather, repeat/spin -> anything), but together they read as a recipe.

=== ANSWER TO THE RESEARCH QUESTION (this setup: distilgpt2, layer 3, last-token
    cosine objective, one prompt, one seed, one topic) ===
No evidence of a text-delivered equivalent of activation steering that works
independently of the text's surface. The effect we saw is predominantly LEXICAL:
 1. Entering the natural hidden-state band WITHOUT topic-specific tokens did not make the
    continuation topical at all (SA: 0.172, off-topic). In Phase 2, the "topicality
    switches on when the state enters the band" pattern only held while topical tokens
    were allowed. It was confounded by them.
 2. Where topicality appears under the semantic block (S), it coincides with
    compositional surface cues: recipe-instruction vocabulary that a per-token
    semantic filter cannot catch, because the topic emerges only from the combination.
    That is still the text's surface, not a latent-only channel.
 3. Hidden-state proximity at one position is a necessary-but-not-sufficient proxy:
    in every run it can be driven below the reference range while the continuation is
    off-topic.
Caveats (why this is not a general negative result): toy model (82M), a single
early layer, a single position (last token), one prompt/seed/topic. A larger model, a
later layer or a multi-position objective could behave differently. Not tested.
